# diar-native — copy to .env and edit.   cp .env.example .env
#
# `./start.sh` creates this file for you and prompts for the token, so you only need to
# edit it by hand if you want something other than the defaults.
#
# Everything below is optional EXCEPT HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN, and even that is only needed for
# the one-time provisioning step. Once the models are on disk, serving needs no token.
#
# The authoritative reference for every DIAR_*/SPEAKRS_*/HF_* variable — what reads it,
# what it does, what it defaults to — is README.md section 6e. Nothing is listed here that
# does not have a read site in the code.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. The one you have to set
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your OWN HuggingFace read token: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
#
# The diarization models are derivatives of the gated pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
# weights, which cannot legally be redistributed — so every operator exports them locally with
# their own token. Accept the terms once, signed in as this token's account, at
#   https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
# It is an email-capture form, auto-approved, and the pipeline is CC-BY-4.0 and free.
#
# Check the token without downloading anything:  ./start.sh --check-token
# Read by: provision-models, check-token. (HF_TOKEN and HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN also work.)
HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN=

# Base URL for the HuggingFace API. The only knob that makes provisioning work against a
# mirror or an air-gapped proxy. Leave unset for huggingface.co.
#HF_ENDPOINT=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Compose-level only — these configure THIS docker-compose.yml, not the binary
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately kept separate from the variables above: no Rust code reads any of these.
# They expand into image tags, published ports and bind-mount sources.

# Image tags. Both are built locally by ./start.sh on first run. Set DIAR_IMAGE to a
# published tag to skip the build.
#DIAR_IMAGE=diar-native:local
#DIAR_PROVISION_IMAGE=diar-native-provision:local

# Host port for the sidecar. The container always listens on 8701.
#DIAR_PORT=8701

# Host directory holding the exported models (~484 MB). Mounted READ-ONLY for serving and
# read-write only by the `provision` profile.
#DIAR_MODELS_HOST_DIR=./models

# Host directory with audio you want to diarize, mounted read-only at /audio.
#DIAR_AUDIO_HOST_DIR=./audio

# HuggingFace cache, so a re-export does not re-download. Only used while provisioning.
#DIAR_HF_CACHE_HOST_DIR=./.hf-cache

# The uid:gid the PROVISIONING container runs as. Defaults to your own, which is what makes
# the exported models land owned by you with no chown and no sudo. The serving container
# ignores this and runs as the image's built-in non-root user, uid/gid 10001:10001.
# ./start.sh sets these automatically from `id -u` / `id -g`.
#DIAR_UID=1000
#DIAR_GID=1000

# Which GPU to reserve, when started with the GPU overlay (docker-compose.gpu.yml).
#DIAR_GPU_DEVICE_ID=0


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Serving knobs (read by `diar-server` with no subcommand)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Devices to load, comma-separated; the FIRST entry is the default for requests that do not
# name one. Wins over DIAR_MODE. `cuda,cpu` loads both and lets each request pick via the
# `device` field. An unknown or not-compiled-in name is FATAL at startup.
# ./start.sh sets this to `cuda,cpu` when it finds a working GPU, `cpu` otherwise.
#DIAR_DEVICES=cpu

# Legacy single-device knob, used only when DIAR_DEVICES is absent. Note the quirk: unset
# OR UNRECOGNIZED falls through to `cuda`, so a typo here does not do what you expect.
# Prefer DIAR_DEVICES.
#DIAR_MODE=cpu

# Global admission gate — bounds TOTAL in-flight requests across all devices.
# WARNING: 0 is accepted and deadlocks every request.
#DIAR_MAX_INFLIGHT=2

# Optional inner sub-gate for CPU work only. Unparseable or 0 is treated as unset.
#DIAR_MAX_INFLIGHT_CPU=

# Assert which tier the startup gate requires: fast | small. Unset reads it from the models
# directory's own marker, falling back to `fast`.
#DIAR_MODEL_SET=fast

# Cap in seconds on the clip fed to the wav2vec2 gender classifier, taken from the middle of
# the window. Unbounded turns cost ~6.3 GB VRAM. Unparseable or 0 falls back to 5.
#DIAR_GENDER_MAX_SECONDS=5

# Downgrade the startup model gate's fatal cases to warnings. Accepts exactly 1, true, TRUE
# or yes — note that `True` does NOT work. Leave off unless you are debugging.
#DIAR_ALLOW_UNVERIFIED_MODELS=

# tracing filter. UNSET DOES NOT MEAN SILENT — the default is `info,ort::logging=warn`.
# ONNX Runtime's native bridge is pinned at warn because it emits ~5800 INFO lines per CUDA
# startup. `speakrs=debug` adds per-stage engine timings.
#RUST_LOG=info,ort::logging=warn

# text (human) or json (one flattened object per line, for an aggregator).
#DIAR_LOG_FORMAT=text


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. Engine tuning (read by speakrs) — leave alone unless you are short on VRAM
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Skip building the batch-64 sessions the CUDA multimask pipeline never runs. Each idle
# session pins its own ORT arena, so this is the cheap VRAM win. Recommended: 1.
#SPEAKRS_LAZY_SESSIONS=1

# Shrink the device arena after each big batched run — a VRAM floor for 4 GB-tier cards, at
# roughly a 20% per-job cost. Off by default; turn on only if you are actually OOMing.
#SPEAKRS_ARENA_SHRINK=

# Thread counts. Defaults are min(cores, 6) / min(cores, 4) / min(cores, 8).
#SPEAKRS_INTRA_THREADS=
#SPEAKRS_FBANK_THREADS=
#SPEAKRS_AHC_THREADS=
